  "problem": {
    "id": "train-3103",
    "question": "Taegan goes to a carnival where she wins tickets from each of the 5 carnival games and also finds 5 tickets on the floor. Each ticket is worth $3. In total, she has tickets that total a value of $30. If Taegan won an equal number of tickets from each of the games, how many tickets did she win from each game?",
    "gold": "1",
    "answer": "If tickets are valued at $3 then in total, Taegan has won $30 in total tickets / $3 per ticket = <<30/3=10>>10 tickets.\nSome of these tickets were found so only 10 total tickets – 5 found tickets = <<10-5=5>>5 tickets were won from carnival games.\nShe therefore won 5 tickets / 5 carnival games = <<5/5=1>>1 ticket from each game.\n#### 1"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many tickets Taegan won from each game, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of tickets Taegan has:**\n   Taegan finds 5 tickets on the floor and each ticket is worth $3. Therefore, the total value of the tickets she finds is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ tickets} \\times 3 \\text{ dollars/ticket} = 15 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n   Since the total value of all her tickets is $30, the value of the tickets she wins from the games is:\n   \\[\n   30 \\text{ dollars} - 15 \\text{ dollars} = 15 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n   Since each ticket is worth $3, the total number of tickets she wins from the games is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{15 \\text{ dollars}}{3 \\text{ dollars/ticket}} = 5 \\text{ tickets}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine how many tickets she won from each game:**\n   Taegan wins an equal number of tickets from each of the 5 games. Therefore, the number of tickets she wins from each game is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{5 \\text{ tickets}}{5 \\text{ games}} = 1 \\text{ ticket/game}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of tickets Taegan won from each game is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
